  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Figure-eights through the gates",
  "description": "Set out 6–8 cone gates, 2–4 metres wide, in an area of about 20 × 20 metres. Everyone has a ball. Dribble around the area, pick a free gate, and dribble a figure of eight round its two cones: through the gate, round one cone, through again and round the other. Then head off to another gate.\n\nMake it harder with left foot only, outside of the foot only, or a challenge: how many figure-eights can you do in a minute? The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Small touches near the cones, longer touches between the gates."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Use both the inside and the outside of the foot."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Look up – which gate is free?"
    }
  ],
